        "original_id": "240d6f9c-357c-5645-8b38-eb9279a47d67",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Glenn Hughes, Dave Evans, Bon Scott, Colin Burgess, George Young, Malcolm Young, Angus Young\n- Bands: Trapeze, Deep Purple, Black Sabbath, AC/DC, Masters Apprentices, The Easybeats\n- Albums: From Now On...\n- Songs: Can I Sit Next to You, Girl\n\nFacts:\n- Glenn Hughes was born on 21 August 1951 and is an English rock bassist and vocalist.\n- Dave Evans was born on 20 July 1953 and is an Australian singer.\n- In 1973–1974, Dave Evans briefly sang for the hard rock band AC/DC.\n- Glenn Hughes is best known for playing bass and performing vocals for Trapeze and for later work with Deep Purple and Black Sabbath.\n- From Now On... is a solo studio album by Glenn Hughes, who was formerly a bassist and vocalist for Deep Purple, Black Sabbath, and Trapeze.\n- On the song \"Can I Sit Next to You, Girl,\" Dave Evans performed the lead vocals before he was replaced by Bon Scott.\n- On the song \"Can I Sit Next to You, Girl,\" Colin Burgess played drums.\n- On the song \"Can I Sit Next to You, Girl,\" George Young played bass guitar and was the older brother of Malcolm Young and Angus Young.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "69986ca1-257b-56f9-8cca-48813cff44a3",
        "text": "Page: Glenn Hughes. Sentence: Glenn Hughes (born 21 August 1951) is an English rock bassist and vocalist, best known for playing bass and performing vocals for funk rock pioneers Trapeze, the Mk.\nPage: Dave Evans (singer). Sentence: Dave Evans (born 20 July 1953) is an Australian singer who briefly sang for the hard rock band AC/DC in 1973–1974.\nPage: From Now On.... Sentence: From Now On... is a solo studio album by former Deep Purple, Black Sabbath and Trapeze bassist/vocalist Glenn Hughes.\nPage: Can I Sit Next to You, Girl. Sentence: This version has lead vocals performed by Dave Evans prior to his being replaced by Bon Scott, as well as drums by ex-Masters Apprentices member Colin Burgess and bass guitar by ex-The Easybeats member George Young (older brother of band cofounders Malcolm Young & Angus Young; co-producer).",
